  || chr(10) || 'Say the national picture first and the state''s in-school sitting second: the in-school sitting is an exception to the national calendar, not the way into the explanation.'
  || chr(10) || 'State only what the section says, with the school year it covers and the day we read the state''s page, and say that a state can change this from year to year and that the state''s own page is where to confirm it.'
  || chr(10) || 'Read school_year_basis before you say the year: where it is the state''s own stated year say so, and where it is the year we read the page in say that instead — never present ours as theirs.'
  || chr(10) || 'Where the section says the state pays, say the family does not pay for that sitting; where it says nothing about who pays, say we do not know who pays.'
  || chr(10) || 'The section is about the state and never about their school: never say their school runs a test day, never name an in-school test date, and never read a state programme as a school''s plan.'
  || chr(10) || 'The ONE exception, and only when school_must_offer is true: the state requires every public high school to hold the sitting, so you may say the day will be held at their school — and where it is null say nothing either way, because null means we did not read it and never that the state does not require it.'
  || chr(10) || 'You may ask once, plainly, whether their school runs it and when — nothing waits on the answer, "I don''t know" is a complete answer, and you never ask again.'
